# Long document and pagination #long-document

::toc {title="Document index" depth="3"}
::toc

This document exists to exercise scrolling, heading navigation, internal links, semantic text, and page estimation. It has enough content to make the Pages toggle meaningful in the playground.

## Chapter 1 #chapter-1

The first chapter establishes stable anchors and normal prose flow. It includes a note and a compact table.

::note {type="tip"}
Checkpoint 1: the renderer should keep the preview and inspector responsive.
::note

| Metric | Value | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Chapter | 1 | stable id chapter-1 |
| Paragraphs | 3 | long document sample |
| Page break | no | preview only |

## Chapter 2 #chapter-2

Longer paragraphs should remain readable before and after page simulation. This paragraph repeats normal prose structure so the host can split content without changing the AST or semantic projection.

::note
Checkpoint 2: page simulation is a host preview feature, not the canonical document model.
::note

| Metric | Value | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Chapter | 2 | stable id chapter-2 |
| Paragraphs | 3 | long document sample |
| Page break | after chapter | preview only |

::pagebreak
::pagebreak

## Chapter 3 #chapter-3

After an explicit page break, rendering continues with the same heading and table behavior.

::note {type="tip"}
Checkpoint 3: page breaks remain ordinary nodes in the AST.
::note

